    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ligatures:none;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-GB;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The proposed signage, by reason of its siting\r\nwould result in an obtrusive, cluttered, incongruous appearance, which would\r\nfail to respect the character of the host dwelling house and the street scene.\r\nIt would therefore fail to preserve public amenity, contrary to the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2023); policy DM5 of the Development Management\r\nPolicies Local plan (2013); and Policy D8 of The London Plan (2021).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
